  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN space stations orbiting around the Earth, and CiC_iCi​ indicates the maximum capacity the ithi^{th}ith station can hold.\n\nAdditionally, there are QQQ missions that must be carried out. Each mission has two requirements: a crew requirement XXX and a storage requirement YYY.\n\nThe crew must all stay in a single cabin, while the other N−1N-1N−1 cabins can be used for storage.\n\nIf cabin iii is chosen for the crew to stay in, the following conditions must be satisfied:\n\n\nX≤CiX \\leq C_iX≤Ci​, so that there's enough space for the entire crew.\nYYY should not exceed the sum of the other N−1N-1N−1 elements of CCC, i.e. C1+C2+…+Ci−1+Ci+1+…+CNC_1 + C_2 + \\ldots + C_{i-1} + C_{i+1} + \\ldots + C_NC1​+C2​+…+Ci−1​+Ci+1​+…+CN​, to satisfy the storage condition.\nIt's possible that no valid choice of cabin exists. To meet the demands of a mission, we can expand the capacity of any space station by spending 111 token per additional unit of capacity.\n\nThat is, using one token, you can increase any single CiC_iCi​ by 111.\n\nFor each mission, determine the minimum number of tokens needed to ensure that there exists a choice of crew cabin which satisfies both conditions. Under the constraints, it can be proven to be always possible.\n\nNote that each mission is to be processed independently, considering the initial capacities CCC.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT, the number of test cases.\nEach test case contains of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains one integer NNN — the number of space stations.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​ — the space station capacities.\nThe third line contains one integer QQQ — the number of missions.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers XiX_iXi​ and YiY_iYi​, denoting the parameters of the iii-th mission.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output QQQ space-separated integers, where the ithi^{th}ith integer represents the minimum tokens needed for the ithi^{th}ith mission.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq Q \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ci,Xi,Yi≤1091 \\leq C_i, X_i, Y_i \\leq 10^91≤Ci​,Xi​,Yi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
